{
  "$schema": "./SCHEMA.md#identity-id",
  "description": "Self-certifying identity id (avalon_protocol::identity_id): identity_id = lowercase_hex(SHA-256(domain tag || ed25519 public key, 32 raw bytes)), the full 256 bits as exactly 64 characters of [0-9a-f] with no prefix. The domain tag is the UTF-8 bytes of 'avalon-identity-id-v1'. Parsing is strict and never normalises: uppercase, 'id:' or 'node:' prefixes and UUID text are rejected. A length other than 64 UTF-8 bytes is an unknown id scheme (a future scheme must use a different length and its own domain tag), reported apart from a malformed id of length 64. Parse vectors carry expected.result: valid, invalid_id or unknown_id_scheme (with expected.length, the UTF-8 byte length); expected.valid is kept. Key acceptability (kind key_acceptability) is the shared Ed25519 policy: canonical encoding and not of small order; a torsion-component key such as y = 3 is accepted. The id differs from the node: shard id for the same key (kind distinct_from_shard_id). Encodings: a public key is lowercase HEX inside signing bytes and standard BASE64 on the wire.",
  "domainTagHex": "6176616c6f6e2d6964656e746974792d69642d7631",
  "domainTagUtf8": "avalon-identity-id-v1",
  "generation": "Deterministic. Seeds are Ed25519 seeds (all bytes equal); publicKeyHex is the derived public key; preimageHex is domainTagHex followed by the key bytes.",
  "supportedIn": [
    "rust",
    "csharp",
    "typescript"
  ],
